okf_version: "1.0"
task: "User: 여전히 유사한에러 ... (Codex TUI through the Ciel Router in G:\\ciel-bridge-service: every shell attempt ends 'aborted' / 'unsupported call', so the agent cannot run anything)."
symptom:
  client_text: "exec -> 'aborted' in the TUI; browser/wait tools -> 'unsupported call'."
  client_log: "~/.codex/logs_2.sqlite, codex_core::tools::router ERROR rows for thread 01a08e99 (20:56:54, 23:17:16-48): tool_name=exec error='Fatal error: tool exec invoked with incompatible payload'; tool_name=js error='unsupported call: js'; tool_name=sleep error='unsupported call: sleep'."
  item_shape: "The rollout records the items the client received: function_call name=exec arguments={\"input\": …} (a function payload for a code-mode custom tool) and function_call name=js|sleep with no namespace field."
root_cause:
  measurement: "Captured the client request of that very thread (app-server thread/resume against a local capture server; no router, no upstream): input[0] carries the Responses Lite catalogue — namespaces functions (exec custom, wait, request_user_input, request_user_input_async) and clock (sleep) — and top-level tools is null. The replayed history in the same body holds 50+ tool calls under the BARE names (function_call name=exec …), only a few with a namespace field."
  conversion: "openai_responses_to_anthropic_messages converted every replayed call to a tool_use under its stored name (exec x46, js x9, sleep x4, wait x1) while the declaration list used the aliased wire names (functions__exec, clock__sleep). The model echoes its history, so it answered with the bare names (live upstream calls are bare)."
  projection: "anthropic_message_to_openai_response resolves a tool_use name only through the alias (functions__exec). A bare name therefore projected to a plain function_call with no namespace and no custom typing — the shape the client rejects. Verified offline with the live body: 'functions__exec' -> custom_tool_call name=exec namespace=functions input=<raw> (the client executed exactly this shape successfully earlier, rollout ctc_fd2ffa2a_1 status completed), while bare 'exec' -> function_call; bare 'sleep'/'js' -> no namespace, which the client answers with 'unsupported call'."
fix:
  request_side: "protocols/openai_responses.py: _replayed_tool_call_name() names a replayed call the way the current request declares it — the item's namespace field when present, otherwise the unique catalogue member with that bare name (undeclared names are left exactly as recorded). The upstream history and the declaration now agree."
  response_side: "anthropic_message_to_openai_response and _custom_tool_source fall back to _namespace_member_identity()/_custom_member_source(): a bare member name restores its namespace and custom-tool contract, so a model echoing a bare name still produces the item the client can run."
verification:
  unit: "tests/test_responses_input_compatibility.py::LiteCatalogueToolIdentityTests (6) — bare custom member projects as custom_tool_call with namespace+raw input; bare member of another namespace keeps its namespace; aliased path unchanged; undeclared names untouched; replayed bare calls convert to functions__exec/clock__sleep; a namespaced item uses its namespace. unit group 1506 OK (45 skipped), router group 1139 OK; ruff clean."
  live_equivalent: "Replayed the failing thread (275 MB rollout copy) through an isolated router against the real DeepSeek API with the prompt 'Run the shell command ls via the exec tool': upstream history now carries functions__exec x63, clock__sleep x5, functions__wait x2 (js/js_reset stay bare — undeclared in that catalogue), and the client executed the call — app-server event item type commandExecution, command '\"C:\\\\Program Files\\\\PowerShell\\\\7\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command ls', cwd G:\\ciel-bridge-service."
  trace_capture_note: "The live router was traced with log level TRACE (CONFIG_DIR/log-level, picked up within a second, no restart) which writes requests.jsonl per instance; it recorded tools=null for every live request, confirming the lite catalogue on the wire. Log level restored to DEBUG afterwards."
state: "Working tree; committed. The running session and its router still execute the previous snapshot, so the fix applies to a session relaunched after the next local deploy."
